# Business rules, non-functional requirements, interfaces and use cases for Chapter 3
BRS = [
 ('BR-01', 'Every SOS trigger (manual, automatic, voice) enters one dispatch pipeline. The trigger method is recorded and does not change the channels used.', 'Novel contribution: one shared trigger engine.', 'High'),
 ('BR-02', 'Manual SOS has no countdown. Automatic, voice and duress-phrase triggers start a 20-second countdown that the user cancels by the method chosen in the settings (swiping the cancel control, speaking the safe phrase or typing the safe phrase); if it is cancelled nothing is sent.', 'Protects against false alarms without delaying a deliberate SOS.', 'High'),
 ('BR-03', 'A silent SOS (silent default mode or duress phrase) produces no sound, vibration, visible alert or revealing notification, and dispatch continues; its 20-second countdown is silent in the same way, with no vibration and no on-screen indication. A loud SOS plays the siren until the user stops it.', 'Supports hiding while calling for help.', 'High'),
 ('BR-04', 'An alert is sent to each trustee on every channel that trustee has enabled; if none is enabled, SMS is used. SMS, push and email are automatic. WhatsApp requires the user to confirm the prepared message and is not used in a silent SOS.', 'WhatsApp cannot send a message without user interaction.', 'High'),
 ('BR-05', 'At Tier 1 only SMS is used. At Tiers 2 and 3 all enabled channels are used. A message that cannot be delivered is queued and retried until delivered, and every attempt is logged.', 'Offline-first delivery.', 'High'),
 ('BR-06', 'The SOS location is a fresh fix if one is obtained within 10 seconds; otherwise the last-known cached location is used and its age is stated in the message.', 'An older location is better than none.', 'High'),
 ('BR-07', 'No audio, transcript or classifier output of the detection or voice engines leaves the device.', 'Privacy guarantee given to users.', 'High'),
 ('BR-08', 'The detection and voice engines store no audio. The only stored audio is the evidence recording of BR-23.', 'Privacy guarantee given to users.', 'High'),
 ('BR-09', 'Microphone detection, voice activation and location sharing are off until the user has given consent. Each has its own toggle, which takes effect immediately. The microphone and voice toggles can be changed at any time; location sharing can be switched on at any time and is switched off on the stop-sharing screen after the safe phrase (BR-11).', 'Informed consent.', 'High'),
 ('BR-10', 'Sharing between two people starts only after both have accepted. An invitation expires after 7 days.', 'Bilateral opt-in.', 'High'),
 ('BR-11', 'A member can stop sharing at any time without anyone\'s approval, by speaking the safe phrase on the stop-sharing screen, which unlocks the sharing toggle, and then switching the toggle off. No other member receives any message about it.', 'Unilateral opt-out without confrontation.', 'High'),
 ('BR-12', 'After a member stops sharing, others see only the last published location with its time, labelled "Not live".', 'A stale location cannot be mistaken for live tracking.', 'High'),
 ('BR-13', 'No hidden tracking: every member can see who is sharing, a sharing member sees a persistent indicator, and only a member can resume their own sharing.', 'Prevents covert surveillance.', 'High'),
 ('BR-14', 'Leaving a circle and stopping sharing are separate actions. Leaving removes the membership and deletes the member\'s stored location from the circle.', 'Separates ending membership from pausing.', 'High'),
 ('BR-15', 'A user may submit at most 5 incident reports in 24 hours and no second report within 100 m and one hour. More than 10 reports in one cell within one hour go to moderation.', 'Prevents spam and malicious flagging.', 'Medium'),
 ('BR-16', 'A report is weighted by 0.5 to the power of (age / 90 days). A cell score is the sum of the weights.', 'Shows current risk.', 'Medium'),
 ('BR-17', 'Reports are grouped by geohash cells of precision 7. A cell shows only category counts and never the identity of a reporter.', 'Anonymity of reporters.', 'Medium'),
 ('BR-18', 'A user becomes a Verified Helper only after the user has requested verification and uploaded the required documents and an administrator has reviewed them manually and approved the request; no document is verified automatically. An administrator can revoke it. The identity image is deleted after the decision.', 'Reduces misuse of the helper network.', 'Medium'),
 ('BR-19', 'A help request goes to Verified Helpers within the set radius (default 1 km). The exact location of the requester is shown only to a helper who accepts.', 'Limits exposure of the requester\'s location.', 'Medium'),
 ('BR-20', 'Library content is bundled and its search runs on the device. Search falls back to keyword search when the model is unavailable or the highest similarity is below 0.30.', 'Offline use and privacy of queries.', 'Medium'),
 ('BR-21', 'Directory entries with coordinates are ordered by distance when a location is available; otherwise by category and name.', 'The nearest help is the most useful.', 'Medium'),
 ('BR-22', 'One account exists per phone number and is verified by a one-time code. Logging in on a new device with the same number ends sessions on other devices.', 'Simple identity and lost-device recovery.', 'High'),
 ('BR-23', 'An evidence recording starts on every SOS, is encrypted, is stored only on the device, is never uploaded, and is deleted after the retention period (default 30 days; 7, 30 or 90 selectable).', 'Evidence stays with the user.', 'Medium'),
 ('BR-24', 'If no acknowledgement arrives within 3 minutes of dispatch, a 30-second warning with cancel starts; if it is not cancelled the escalation message goes to the configured authority numbers. Any acknowledgement or a cancel stops the escalation.', 'Follow-through with a safeguard against false escalation.', 'Medium'),
 ('BR-25', 'A missing-child report is active, found or expired. It expires 72 hours after creation or renewal unless the guardian renews it.', 'Reports must not remain active indefinitely.', 'Medium'),
 ('BR-26', 'A child\'s photo is visible only to the guardian, the alerted trustees and the notified helpers while the report is active, and is deleted when the report is found or expired.', 'Child-data privacy.', 'Medium'),
 ('BR-27', 'A user may file at most 3 missing-child reports in 24 hours. Alerts for a report are sent at once, and an administrator reviews every report afterwards. A report removed as false is deleted from all lists, its further alerts stop and its author may be suspended. The application makes no direct connection to official systems.', 'Abuse prevention and clear boundary with official channels.', 'Medium'),
 ('BR-28', 'In Decoy Mode the application shows a neutral calculator; SOS, voice triggers, location updates and evidence recording continue underneath. A 2-second hold on the equals key returns to the real interface.', 'Protects the user when forced to unlock the phone.', 'High'),
 ('BR-29', 'The disguise offers three predefined neutral appearances and does not change functions, data or settings.', 'Disguise must not disable safety.', 'Low'),
 ('BR-30', 'The nearest safe location is the nearest hospital or police station of the bundled directory by straight-line distance; directions are turn-by-turn when online and distance and direction when offline.', 'Works from stored data.', 'Low'),
 ('BR-31', 'Only accounts with the administrator role can use the admin website. Every moderation or review decision is logged with the administrator and the time.', 'Accountability.', 'Medium'),
 ('BR-32', 'A user\'s location is shared only with trustees (SOS), circle members (while sharing), helpers who have accepted, and authority numbers (escalation).', 'Data minimisation.', 'High'),
]

